4) What  action  to  be  made  when  character  is  operand(i.e. '0'  to  '9' )  ?  ---> Push  int(operand)  into  the  stack

5) What  action  to  be  made  when  character  is  operator ? --->  Pop  the  last  two  elements  of  the  stack ,
													 save  them  in  'y'  and  'x'  and
													 push  the  result  of  x  operator  y  into  the  stack

6) What  does  stack  finally  contain ?  ---> Result  of  the  postfix  expression

7) Postfix  expression  is  bracket  free  expression'''

'''
Write  a  program  to  evaluate  postfix  expression

Posifix  expression  --->    3 4 5 * + 6 2 / -
'''
def  eval(a):
	stack=stack()#How  to  create  a  stack  class  object
	for char in a:#How  to  iterate  postfix  expression  with  for  loop:
		if  char.isdigit():
				stack.push(int(char))#How  to  push  the  operand  into  the  stack
		else:
				y=stack.pop()
				x=stack.pop()#How  to  remove  two  values  of  the  stack
				match  char:
					case   '+':  
						stack.push(x+y)#How to  push  addition  result  into  the  stack
					case   '-':  #
						stack.push(x-y)#How to  push  subtraction  result  into  the  stack
					case   '*':  
						stack.push(x*y)#How to  push  product  result  into  the  stack
					case   '/':  
						stack.push(x/y)#How to  push  division  result  into  the  stack
					case   '^':  
						stack.push(x^y)#How to  push  power  result  into  the  stack
	#  End  of  for  loop
	return stack.pop()#return  result  of  expression
#  End  of  the  function
infix=input("Enter infix expression:")#How  to  read  infix  expression
postfix=convert(infix)
print("Postfix expression:",postfix)#How  to  convert infix  to  postfix
res=eval(postfix)
print("Result of expression:",res)#How  to  evaluate  postfix  expression
